te the massive  improvements made after many people  moved on then you'll be satisfied by the  division to an open beta begins on March  1st running until the 4th so once again  try it before you buy it  the main issue most people took from the  last game was the lack of endgame  content so Ubisoft massive have made  this their priority keeping gamers happy  long after the campaign credits roll a  new enemy faction  we found character specializations are  unlocked such as bringing a sniper rifle  so powerful it can one-hit most enemies  but the one which piques my interests  are the new raids which can be played by  up to eight players the problem is I  don't know seven people I'd love to know  your thoughts on the division to which  releases on March 15th on ps4 Xbox and  PC when you think of from software what  games brings to mind  Dark Souls or Demon Souls maybe  blood-borne this company's expertise lie  in appealing to the hardcore gamers who  want to challenge the average gamer will  die over 100 times before finishing  anything from from software the latest  title is Sakura shadows die twice set in  sixteenth century Japan the time of the  shinobi you could be expecting a point  system upgrading specific skills and  carefully managing the abilities that  suit your playstyle things are a little  simpler here in Sakura  don't get me wrong though but nothing  near the depth from previous games  allowing us mere mortals to access the  game without feeling overwhelmed the  main focus of Sakura is to use Paris to  break the opponent's posture when this  is done right they become off-balance  for a moment and the opportunity to  strike presents itself making it  possible to end fights in a single blow  if you ever played the tenchu series  you'll be happy to know it's possible to  play large portions of Sakura using  instant stealth kills as long as you  remain unspotted this adds yet another  layer of tactics to the game look for  guard patterns to exploit or rushing  like a madman fight your own way it's  your choice  Sakura shadows die twice releases on  March 22nd on ps4 PC and the Xbox one  here's something which will confuse the  younger members of the audience  toejam Annelle back in the groove  without context I've got to admit this  game looks absolutely terrible but  toejam and earl is steeped in retro  history the game is based on the  original title from back on the Sega  Genesis or Mega Drive over here from  1991 in solo or co-op you'll search the  island for pieces of your broken rocket  ship and then find an elevator to the  next level rinse and repeat the enemies  you face are based on stereotypes from  single mums with crying babies to a  miniature devil they all can kill you  but worse is if they push you to the  side of the map and you fall down a few  levels making regression a real worry in  later stage  falling down five Maps is possible and  bloody heartbreaking the project was  kick-started and ended with over 500  thousand dollars raised to see toejam  and Earl return if you're under 20 years  old here let me know you have thoughts  does this game make any sense to you  toejam and earl back in the groove  releases on March the first on ps4 Xbox  one switch PC and even the market what's  your favorite fighting game you may be  looking forward to Mortal Kombat 11 or  you may be og and like Street Fighter we  all tend to gravitate towards one over  another one which is quietly doing its  own thing is Dead or Alive now on its  sixth iteration right let's quickly get  something out of the way that DOA is  known for boob physics yep they are  still here and still overly bouncy but  underneath that term tessellation is a  very well-put-together fighter  the expansive story mode with branching  options looks like a great deal of fun  with early playtesters incredibly  impressed by the quest mode which breaks  down fights to concentrate on specific  skills quickly rewarded by costume  unlocks and other aesthetic items as you  can tell the character customization is  here and extremely robust but my  favorite part is the slow-motion damage  cinematics and the way the damage  remains on the character throughout the  fight are you thinking about grabbing  Dead or Alive 6 it releases on March the  1st on ps4 Xbox one PC and you'll even  see it bouncing over on arcade - did you  hear about a battle royale game that  appeared with zero fanfare okay so 25  million people downloaded it so I'm sure  you've heard about apex legends well  this overnight behemoth will release its  first season of content in early March  they intend to do this without  advertising so finding information  before the release is close to  impossible what we do know is that the  Battle Pass will be focused around  visual cosmetics keeping the playing  field even - all will see the roster  increased with 11 names found by leakers  but nothing is confirmed just yet in  addition new weapons will release each  and every season a new loot for everyone  season 1 runs for three months making  June the start of the second season the  pricing structure for the Battle Pass  will be a huge indicator as to the  longevity of the product will we see EA  take control and arguably hurt the game  with Faust microtransactions or will  spawn the developers went out and  control their own product  let's hope is the latter we may have  found the spiritual successor to Metal  Gear Solid left alive the front mission  universe has always had a close tie in  with Metal Gear I remember the exclusive  tank decals from Metal Gear Solid Peace  Walker suddenly turning up in front  mission involved but it's not only that  the themes the stealth action the mech  focus are all here in left alive and  with many of the Metal Gear crew working  on left alive it really feels like an  authentic Metal Gear sub story left  alive is essentially a cover shooter  with a heavy focus on survival but it  includes many of the genres to break up  the core gameplay loop the stealth  options in particular can overshadow The  Stand and Deliver gunplay and allows us  to choose our own approach to each piece  of combat there are sections of mech  combat along the way with the story  spanning three characters so the law and  the narrative is constantly added to but  don't worry it's not as convoluted as  Metal Gear well not yet anyway  left alive released in Japan last month  and hits the rest of the world on March  the fifth on ps4 and xboxone here's  something a little different generation  0 the first thing I want to say about  this game is that it's not full price as  you'd expect it's about 60 percent of  what you usually pay generation 0 is an  open world survival outing which can be  played alone or with friends  cooperatively this is a hostile world so  weapons are very important but the love  of exploration is the core value in  battle thin walls can be shot through  making hiding a risky decision keeping  us on edge as a real survival title  shoot missions are given out regularly  to give us direction during the  livestream the squad was asked to  destroy a gas station which alerted  nearby factions which so happened to be  mixed resulting in a tense gunfight  there are two HD re-releases to quickly  note before we end Assassin's Creed 3  which tells a story of how a Native  American played a key role in the birth  of the USA it's more of the Assassin's  Creed you know and love but with  slightly improved visuals releasing on  March 29th the danganronpa trilogy  rounds out the month again releasing on  March 29th as the title suggests it's  three dunk and romper titles in 1 so if  you've been thinking about trying the  series out now is a perfect time  so there we have it 10 games releasing  over March 2019 are you grabbing  anything I'll likely pick up the apex  legends battle pass for season 1 and  second all looks good and Devil May Cry  5 is bloody good job my wallet is going  to hate me I'm Adam from Pla